       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's well above the maximum metformin dose.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Single doses are typically no more than 1,000 \u03bcg... more precisely, no more than 1,000 mg.\n\nAt 5,100 mg/day, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg at some other frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd add a note on the order documenting that it was intentional."
